jobs.description:
Hey go-getter! Are you looking for a fun, dynamic job in logistics? Do you love it when your workday just flies by, and are you ready to dive into the world of books? Awesome! For CB in Culemborg, we are looking for logistics employees to join their fantastic returns department. You’ll earn an hourly wage starting at €15.49 (19+). Sounds good? Keep on reading!

What we offer
- A starting salary of €15.49 per hour (19+)
- Work together with enthusiastic colleagues
- Attractive allowances for evening shifts
- A 40-hour workweek
- Travel allowance. Always a nice bonus!
- An employer rated with an 8+ for work atmosphere

Who you are
As a logistics employee at CB, you are a team player who just can't sit still. Furthermore, you love staying active and you meet the following requirements:

- You are available to work full-time (40 hours);
- You are available from Monday to Friday and/or Sunday (you don't work on Saturdays);
- You are available in 2 shifts: 07:00-15:30 and 14:00-22:30;
- You speak Dutch or English;
- You are fully available in August and September at the very least, as summer is a very busy period at CB.

What will you do
As a logistics employee at CB, you will be working across various logistics and production processes. No two days are the same! You will be working in the OFM department. This is the ultimate place where, among other things, all returning books arrive. Your tasks will include:

- Packing books and customer orders and getting them completely ready for shipment;
- Picking the right orders—you know exactly where to find everything;
- Processing returns and neatly placing items back into stock;
- Taking care of internal restocking and transport flows.

Where will you work
As a logistics employee returns, you will find yourself in the warehouse of CB. CB is the largest book distribution center in the Netherlands! The company scores an 8+ for work atmosphere. So, it’s super fun! At CB, they organize great staff outings, there’s a lovely compa

As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse operation. Together with your colleagues, you make sure orders are processed efficiently and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Operating an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Loading and unloading goods;
- Checking products for accuracy and completeness;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workplace.

Thanks to a structured onboarding program, you'll quickly learn all aspects of the job.

- Are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Have a basic understanding of Dutch and/or English;
- Enjoy physical and active work;
- Work accurately and responsibly;
- Are motivated and eager to learn.

Previous logistics experience is a plus, but not required.

Are you detail-oriented, quality-focused, and looking for a full-time job in a dynamic logistics environment? Then this opportunity as a Quality Control Employee in Lelystad could be the perfect fit for you!

As a Quality Control Employee, you play a key role in ensuring that products meet the highest quality standards before moving further through the logistics process. You will work in a supportive team environment and be part of a 2-shift schedule (morning and afternoon shifts)

As a Quality Control Employee, your responsibilities include:

- Inspecting products to ensure they meet quality standards;
- Identifying, reporting, and helping resolve product defects;
- Carefully checking products for damages, errors, or irregularities;
- Maintaining a clean and organized work area;
- Contributing to an efficient and high-quality logistics operation;
- Following quality and safety procedures at all times.

- Basic English communication skills are required;
- Full-time availability;
- Strong attention to detail and quality;
- Ability to work effectively in a team environment;
- Ability to follow instructions accurately;
- Previous experience in quality control, production, or logistics is an advantage, but not required.

Are you an experienced Reach Truck Driver looking for a new opportunity? We are currently recruiting for a modern logistics company in Helmond. As a Reach Truck Driver, you will be responsible for safely and efficiently moving goods throughout the warehouse while supporting daily logistics operations using modern equipment.

Your responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck at heights of up to 12 meters;
- Moving and storing pallets throughout the warehouse;
- Picking orders using the reach truck;
- Scanning, labeling, and wrapping pallets;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Supporting Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule may be required. (6:00-15:00/15:00-00:00)

- Holds a valid Reach Truck certificate;
- Is comfortable working at heights up to 12 meters;
- Fulltime available;
- Living nearby Helmond, Mierlo, Geldrop, Nuenen or Eindhoven;
- Has experience in logistics and safety;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English.
